WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.662
Why do so many programs stall
at Initial or low Advanced?

2
00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:08.138
Because they read CISA's maturity
model as a five-pillar shopping list.

3
00:00:08.138 --> 00:00:12.280
But the model runs those pillars
through cross-cutting capabilities,

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.994
and the one programs fund
least is Governance:

5
00:00:14.994 --> 00:00:18.637
defining and enforcing policy
within and across the pillars.

6
00:00:18.637 --> 00:00:21.643
Its Traditional stage
reads like a failure list,

7
00:00:21.643 --> 00:00:25.174
with siloed enforcement and
little correlation of logs.

8
00:00:25.174 --> 00:00:29.313
The book answers with five principles,
and none of them is a purchase.

9
00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:32.971
Identity is the anchor, but
it isn't self-authenticating,

10
00:00:32.971 --> 00:00:37.187
so sessions are re-evaluated and
the identity plane is defended.

11
00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:40.004
Privileged identity gets
controls of its own,

12
00:00:40.004 --> 00:00:44.451
with no standing admin assignments
outside tested emergency accounts.

13
00:00:44.451 --> 00:00:47.738
Evidence must be reproducible
and machine-readable.

14
00:00:47.738 --> 00:00:50.477
Governance enforces; a policy that only

15
00:00:50.477 --> 00:00:53.799
produces next quarter's
finding is just a report.

16
00:00:53.799 --> 00:00:56.963
And the cloud boundary
is modeled, gap by gap.

17
00:00:56.963 --> 00:00:59.470
Next, what the mandates actually say.
